    },
    "message": "Keep serving the queue head while followers move up\n\nprogress_physical_queue_positions and progress_physical_queue_head_to_service\nheld back service whenever anyone in the facility's queue was walking\nto a slot. In a long queue every service shifted the whole line one slot\nat a time, so service rarely started: with 100 people the single meal\nstation started service 65 times in a day while its queue grew to 72.\n\nFollower walks still happen one at a time, but now only the head's own\nwalk delays its service. A follower may arrive after people ahead were\nserved, so its slot can have moved; arrival is accepted at the point it\nwas sent to, and the next tick moves it to its current slot.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
